## Context

While verifying that `make world` reaches every committed handoff
artifact (0415), four tracked files under `report/inputs/generated/`
turned out to have NO producer rule anywhere in the phase makefiles:

- `regimes.csv`
- `tab_exp2_arms_runs.csv`
- `tab_exp2_bib_quality.csv`
- `tab_source_grounding.tex`

Pre-existing: the old root Makefile never reached them either. They are
committed (the 0405 policy tracks the P3 tree) but unreproducible from
the DAG — a gap in the "each phase rebuilds from the previous phase's
tracked outcomes alone" invariant.

## Actions

1. For each file: find its generating script (git log / grep src/ for
   the output filename) and classify — (a) live artifact whose rule was
   lost in a migration → restore a rule in render.mk; (b) consumed by
   report/slides but generator gone → decide regenerate-vs-freeze,
   document; (c) consumed by nothing → retire (git rm, manifest row
   update in docs/pipeline-phases.md).
2. Extend the DAG guard (test_makefile_dag or a small adherence test):
   every tracked file under report/inputs/generated/ has a producer
   rule in render.mk (allowlist for deliberately frozen artifacts, with
   a comment per entry).

## Test

The guard of action 2 — red today (4 files), green after action 1.

## Verification

- [x] Each of the four classified with evidence (producer found or
      consumer absence shown)
- [x] Guard green; make check green; clean-room tests green

## Invariants

- No data content changes without explicit regeneration review (0383)

## Exit criteria

- Zero tracked P3 artifacts without producer rule or documented freeze
- Guard prevents recurrence
